    "result_text": "The configured test suite (which runs `AcceptanceTest`) passes with **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the city-capacity rule: creating an owner is rejected with **409 Conflict** when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nFollowing the codebase's existing collaborator-component pattern (mirroring `NamesakeCounter`, `CustomerCodeAssigner`, etc.), I made two changes:\n\n1. **New component** \u2014 `rest/controller/CityCapacityChecker.java`: a single-responsibility `@Component` with `isCityAtCapacity(Owner)`, reusing the existing `ClinicService.countOwnersByCity(...)` \u2192 `OwnerRepository.countByCity(...)` chain that was already in place. The threshold (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 50`) lives here.\n\n2. **Controller wiring** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1`: injected the checker via the constructor and added the capacity check in `addOwner`, alongside the existing conflict checks and *before* `saveOwner` (so the count excludes the owner being created), returning `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` when the city is full.\n\nNo new exception class or `ControllerAdvice` change was needed \u2014 this matches how every other 409 in this controller is returned (inline `ResponseEntity`). The acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fill a city to 50, then expect the 51st to get 409) passes.",
